WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.936
AI is not magic. It learns useful patterns from examples.

00:00:03.936 --> 00:00:10.627
Imagine predicting ice cream sales from the temperature. Each dot is a day we have already seen.

00:00:10.627 --> 00:00:17.319
At first, our model guesses badly. Training compares its predictions with the real answers, then adjusts its

00:00:17.319 --> 00:00:23.616
numbers to make the errors smaller. Repeat that process, and a useful pattern starts to emerge.

00:00:23.616 --> 00:00:29.520
Neural networks do this with many connected layers. The connections have strengths, called weights, that

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:30.701
change during training.

00:00:30.701 --> 00:00:38.573
Once trained, the model can make predictions about new examples. But a good fit to old data is not enough.

00:00:38.573 --> 00:00:40.541
Test it on new data.

00:00:40.541 --> 00:00:43.690
And remember: a prediction can still be wrong.
